{#
    THE frame for a CommercialDocument's EDIT screen — the sell side's order form, quote form and
    invoice create screen, and the buy side's purchase order form, once.
    `admin/order/form.html.twig`, `admin/estimate/form.html.twig`, `admin/invoice/create.html.twig`
    and `@Procurement/purchase_order_edit.html.twig` extend this and fill its blocks. The name
    matches the PHP interface every one of these documents implements — `Invoice`, `SalesOrder`,
    `Estimate`, `CreditMemo` and `PurchaseOrder` — rather than claiming to be sales-only when a
    purchase document extends it too.

    PurchaseOrder does not use the customer-chooser step below at all: it always renders the full
    workspace directly (`workspaceReady` is always true for it), vendor being chosen inline or via
    `?vendor=`. Nothing here is branched on that fact — it simply never fills `picker_step` or
    `company_picker_options`.

    ## The rule this template is built on

    PARAMETERS AND BLOCKS, NEVER `{% if document == 'invoice' %}`. Nothing below asks which document
    it is rendering. A difference arrives as a value set at the top of the child, as a block the
    child fills, or — where it is a whole region with a context of its own — as a TEMPLATE PATH,
    which is what `admin/invoice/create.html.twig` already does with its `contextTemplate` and
    `chargeTemplate` and what the line table does with its `actionsTemplate`. A difference that can
    be expressed none of those ways belongs in the child, not in a branch here.

    ## EDIT ONLY, and why it is not the view base

    There are two bases. `commercial_document_view.html.twig` is the read-only one; this is the one that
    posts. "Edit and view can be quite different", and they are:

      * NO CUSTOMISATION SKELETON. The view base carries a stable slug per region, two predefined
        `injection_point()`s and a written-down register of which regions a stored layout may
        eventually move. None of that is here, deliberately: "the user customization only affects
        view / edit is pretty much the same and set by us", and "view formatting doesn't wipe data".
        A movable region on a screen that SAVES is a way to lose a field, so this frame is fixed and
        ours. The blocks below are fill points, not slots — no layout may reorder them, and none is
        a public name anything outside these four files may bind to.

      * IT OWNS A FORM. The frame opens the `<form>`, prints the CSRF field, and closes the form
        around everything a save reads. The view base renders no form control at all.

      * IT HAS TWO STATES. A sell-side edit screen is two pages behind one route: step one is the
        customer chooser, and step two is the workspace. `workspaceReady` is which, and the chooser
        is part of the frame because all three screens open with the same one.

      * THE FRAME IS THE SALES ORDER'S. Where the three disagreed about the shape of a region, the
        order won — "sales order is golden standard".

    ## The frame, in order

        region                what it is                                           fill point
        ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        no-JS rules           the progressive-enhancement style pair                2 blocks
        hero                  eyebrow, heading (+ this document's status), lead,    parameters
                              and this document's own buttons                       + 2 blocks
        tab_nav               the edit screen's own tab bar                         block
        ── the workspace shell ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        form                  the workspace card the whole save posts from          parameters
        form_head             hidden identity fields and the banners                block
        top_actions           the action row above the grid                         block
        context               the document's own fields, addresses, custom fields   block
        ── the line-items section ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        lines_heading                                                               parameter
        lines_toolbar         the add-line controls that sit above the table         block
        lines_note            what an admin needs to know before typing a line       block
        lines_table           the one table, already a shared component              block
        lines_after_table     see the note on that block                            block
        lines_footer          the add-line bar and the totals box                    block
        footerNote            the right-aligned note under them                      parameter
        bottom_actions        this document's buttons again, at the bottom           block
        ── after the form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        after_form            sections that are not part of the save                block
        page_end              modals and <template>s — last because that is what     block
                              they are
        ── or, where no customer has been chosen yet ──────────────────────────────────────────
        picker_step           step one, identical on all three sell-side screens —   2 blocks
                              default body is today's bare customer chooser

    Line items and the totals box are NOT movable and are not offered as anything a layout could
    reposition — "that block is solid", and "fees, shipping, tax, totals — i don't think users
    should just drag that around either. pretty fixed". They are named here so that the frame can
    say where they go, and that is all the names do.

    Parameters (set at the top of the child, outside its blocks)
    -----------------------------------------------------------
    workspaceReady      required  a customer is resolved, so there is a document to build. False
                                  renders step one — the customer chooser — and nothing else.
    formId              required when workspaceReady. The workspace form's id; the buttons in the
                                  hero post it by `form="..."`, so it is not free to drift.
    formClass           optional  extra classes on the workspace card, for a document whose form
                                  carries a script hook.
    formAction          optional  the workspace form's action. Absent posts to the current URL,
                                  which is what the order form does and has always done.
    heroEyebrow         optional  the small word above the heading.
    heroLead            optional  the sentence under it. Absent renders no <p> at all.
    linesHeading        optional  the <h2> above the line table. Absent renders no heading, which
                                  is the order form's shape.
    footerNote          optional  the right-aligned note under the totals box.
    pickerAction        optional  step one's form action. Absent posts to the current URL.
    pickerSelectClass   optional  a script hook on step one's customer <select>.
    pickerSelectPlaceholder optional  its data-placeholder.

    Blocks
    ------
    Every block above, all empty by default except the two no-JS style blocks, which default to the
    pair the order form and the quote form both use.

    `hero_heading` carries the <h1> AND, where the document has one, the status control beside it —
    the order's status, the quote's acceptance status. It is one block rather than a heading block
    plus a status block because the order wraps the two in a flex row of its own, and a frame that
    imposed that wrapper on the other two would restyle their headings. The other home for a
    document's status is a row in its info card, which is inside `context`.

    `form_attributes` is printed INSIDE the <form> tag, for the data-* attributes a document's own
    script reads. It is a block and not a map of parameters so that each attribute is written, and
    escaped, exactly as it was before this frame existed — see the snapshot note below.

    `picker_step` wraps the WHOLE of step one — the `<section class="order-company-card">` and the
    form inside it, "Choose Customer" label included — and defaults to exactly that markup, so the
    order form, the quote form and the invoice create screen keep overriding only the innermost
    `company_picker_options` exactly as before and never need to touch `picker_step` itself. It
    exists so a document whose step one is not about a company has somewhere to put its own picker
    without inheriting customer-specific wording — nothing does yet, and PurchaseOrder does not use
    this branch at all (see above).

    ## The snapshot boundary

    Nothing here prints a line value. `LineDenomination::boxUntouched()` compares a box against its
    hidden `*_rendered` twin BYTE FOR BYTE to tell "nobody touched this" from "somebody retyped the
    same number", so a figure that came back through a filter turns a round trip that should change
    nothing into a rewrite of a stored figure. The frame owns wrappers; the values inside them are
    the shared line row's business and are passed through untouched.
#}
{% extends 'admin/_main/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block admin_body %}
    {# ── the no-JS rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       The add/remove controls that need scripting are hidden without it, and the server-rendered
       spare rows and submit fallbacks take over. Two blocks rather than one so that a document
       adding a rule to the <noscript> half does not have to restate the other. #}
    <style>
        {% block no_js_style %}.no-js-row, .no-js-inline { display: none; }{% endblock %}
    </style>
    <noscript>
        <style>
            {% block no_js_noscript_style %}
            .no-js-row { display: table-row !important; }
            .no-js-inline { display: inline-block !important; }
            .js-only { display: none !important; }
            {% endblock %}
        </style>
    </noscript>

    {# ── hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="panel compact-panel">
        <div class="panel-title-row">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">{{ heroEyebrow|default('') }}</p>
                {% block hero_heading %}{% endblock %}
                {% if heroLead|default('') %}<p class="lead">{{ heroLead }}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            <div class="panel-actions">
                {% block hero_actions %}{% endblock %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── tab_nav ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% block tab_nav %}{% endblock %}

    <section class="order-create-shell">
        {% if workspaceReady %}
            <form method="post" id="{{ formId }}" class="order-workspace-card{% if formClass|default('') %} {{ formClass }}{% endif %}"{% if formAction|default('') %} action="{{ formAction }}"{% endif %}{% block form_attributes %}{% endblock %}>
                {{ csrf_field() }}

                {# ── form_head — the hidden identity fields, and the banners that ride a save ── #}
                {% block form_head %}{% endblock %}

                {# ── top_actions — captured rather than printed in place, so a document with no
                       action row above the grid is not given an empty one. ── #}
                {% set topActions %}{% block top_actions %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
                {% if topActions|trim is not empty %}
                    <div class="order-workspace-actions">{{ topActions }}</div>
                {% endif %}

                {# ── context — the document's own fields, its addresses and its custom fields.
                       Whole, because the invoice create screen delegates this to one of two
                       `contextTemplate`s that each open a workspace grid of their own. ── #}
                {% block context %}{% endblock %}

                {# ── the line-items section — FIXED, and so is the totals box inside its footer ── #}
                <section class="order-lines-section">
                    {% if linesHeading|default('') %}<h2>{{ linesHeading }}</h2>{% endif %}
                    {% block lines_toolbar %}{% endblock %}
                    {% block lines_note %}{% endblock %}

                    <div class="wide-table-wrap">
                        {% block lines_table %}{% endblock %}
                    </div>

                    {# Between the table and the footer. Only the invoice create screen fills it,
                       with the submit that adds a row server-side; the order form and the quote
                       form put their add controls ABOVE the table, in `lines_toolbar`. That
                       disagreement is real and predates this frame — nothing is moved here. #}
                    {% block lines_after_table %}{% endblock %}

                    <div class="order-lines-footer">
                        {% block lines_footer %}{% endblock %}
                    </div>

                    {% if footerNote|default('') %}
                        <p class="lead" style="margin:8px 0 0; text-align:right;">{{ footerNote }}</p>
                    {% endif %}

                    <div class="order-bottom-actions">
                        {% block bottom_actions %}{% endblock %}
                    </div>
                </section>
            </form>

            {# ── after_form — what is on the page but not part of the save ── #}
            {% block after_form %}{% endblock %}

            {# ── page_end — modals and <template>s ── #}
            {% block page_end %}{% endblock %}
        {% else %}
            {# ── step one: nothing but the customer chooser ────────────────────
               A customer decides the price list, the addresses a save freezes and the party
               billed, so none of the three screens renders a workspace before there is one.
               Posting company_id and nothing else is answered with a redirect carrying the
               customer back, which is the redirect-then-reload that makes this work with
               scripting off. #}
            {% block picker_step %}
                <section class="order-company-card">
                    <form method="post" class="order-company-picker"{% if pickerAction|default('') %} action="{{ pickerAction }}"{% endif %}>
                        {{ csrf_field() }}
                        <label for="company_id">Choose Customer <span class="req">*</span></label>
                        <div class="order-company-select">
                            <select id="company_id" name="company_id"{% if pickerSelectClass|default('') %} class="{{ pickerSelectClass }}"{% endif %}{% if pickerSelectPlaceholder|default('') %} data-placeholder="{{ pickerSelectPlaceholder }}"{% endif %} required>
                                <option value=""></option>
                                {% block company_picker_options %}{% endblock %}
                            </select>
                        </div>
                        <button class="button primary" type="submit">Next</button>
                    </form>
                </section>
            {% endblock %}
        {% endif %}
    </section>
{% endblock %}
